# Per-round health-check output (round 241/247): reproducible by
# re-running harness/run_tests_fast.sh or languages/whence/run_tests_fast.sh
# directly, and driver.log already carries the PASS/FAIL summary line —
# these full logs are diagnostic scratch, not source, growing one file per
# round forever if left tracked.
logs/health_round_*.log
logs/whence_health_round_*.log
# Round 365 (SWE-loop D) pre-flight reconciliation: round 363 wired a THIRD
# per-round health log (`skills/run_checks_fast.sh` -> corpus-check) into
# run_driver.sh but did not extend this pattern, so round 364's log landed in
# `git status` as an unattributed `??` and tripped round 365's record-gap
# check. Same class as the two lines above, same reasoning verbatim.
logs/skills_health_round_*.log
# Round 441 (skills B): a FIFTH per-round log. `run_driver.sh:649` writes
# `logs/slowtier_round_<N>.log` for every round the slow-tier slice runs in,
# and the wiring round did not extend this pattern -- so round 440's log
# landed in `git status` as an unattributed `??` and tripped round 441's
# record-gap check, which is the third time in a row (rounds 363/365,
# 409, and now) that a per-round log was wired without its ignore line.
# Same class and same reasoning as the four patterns above: the DURABLE
# artefact is `state/slow-tier-ledger.jsonl`, which is tracked; this is the
# slice's own progress log and `driver.log` already carries its summary line.
#
# Checked before adding, because an ignore line is read by more than
# `git status` (see this round's knowledge file): the ONLY in-tree reader of
# `logs/slowtier_round_*` is the `run_driver.sh` line that WRITES it --
# `git grep -n slowtier_round` returns that one source hit plus two prose
# citations in `state/research-state.md`. Nothing selects on its git status,
# so ignoring it silences no measurement.
logs/slowtier_round_*.log

# Round 409 (harness A) wired a FOURTH per-round health log
# (`nuc/run_checks_fast.sh` -> nuc-health-check). Extended in the SAME
# round as the wiring, which is the whole point of round 365's note
# above: round 363 wired the third check without this line, and the
# next round's log landed in `git status` as an unattributed `??` and
# tripped the record-gap check.
logs/nuc_health_round_*.log

# Round 463 (harness A): retained output of a NOT-CLEAN corpus checker,
# `logs/corpus-evidence/round-<N>/<check>.out`, written by
# `skills/skill-authoring/scripts/corpus_check.py` (`_attach_evidence`).
# Same class and same reasoning as the five per-round-log patterns above,
# and added in the SAME round as the wiring on purpose: rounds 363/365, 409
# and 441 each wired a per-round log WITHOUT its ignore line and each left
# the next round an unattributed `??` that tripped the record-gap check.
# Three instances of one avoidable mistake is enough.
#
# Checked before adding, per round 441's rule that an ignore line is read by
# more than `git status`: `git grep -n corpus-evidence` at the time of
# writing returned only this round's own PREDICTIONS.md, so no measurement
# selects on this path's git status and ignoring it silences nothing. The
# DURABLE artefacts stay tracked as always -- the round file, the knowledge
# file, and `driver.log`'s `skills-check FAIL` line, which now carries the
# retained path because `evidence:` lines print above the summary and
# `driver_line` joins the last five.
#
# Note this is DIAGNOSTIC SCRATCH BY CONSTRUCTION: it exists only for rounds
# whose corpus check was already red, and a green repo never creates the
# directory at all.
logs/corpus-evidence/

