# Round 352: the swap-watch supervisor's live poll log. It is appended to once
# a minute for the run's whole duration (8h), so tracking it would leave a
# genuinely uncommitted diff in `git status` for every round in that window and
# trip the record-gap check eight times over for a file that is doing exactly
# what it is supposed to. The DURABLE artifacts of a run -- the checkpoint
# JSONL and the final JSON the watcher scp's back -- are tracked as normal;
# only the supervisor's own progress log is ignored.
state/nuc-swap-watch-*/poll.log

# Whence example programs written by the Hermes gateway, a SEPARATE
# autonomous system that shares this repo. They are listed in
# state/known-standing-dirty-paths.json as permanently untracked and have
# been since round 291; round 393's `git add -A` sweep (49969fb) tracked
# all fourteen anyway, which put the repo's own two records in
# contradiction. Ten of the fourteen do not parse under v0.19's braced-
# block rule, and tests/test_v26.py filters on `git ls-files` precisely so
# that this program's corpus is the one in git — so tracking them made a
# whence_slow test red for nine rounds. Round 402 untracked them; these
# entries are what stops the next `git add -A` from re-tracking them.
# The FILES ARE STILL ON DISK and are still read as the cure system's
# field corpus by curecheck.py, tests/test_v22.py, test_v33.py, test_v34.py
# and test_field_corpus_selector.py, none of which care about tracking.
# Round 444 added the FIFTEENTH, agi_buy_and_hold.lang (gateway-written
# 2026-09-01 23:12 UTC), in the same commit that DECLARED it in the new
# membership roster state/whence/round-444/field-roster.json. That order
# is round 441's rule and it is not cosmetic: `curecheck.field_corpus_
# drift()` computes `untracked - declared`, so an ignore line alone
# turns a real drift report green by hiding the file from git rather
# than by declaring it. Ignore only what is already declared.
languages/whence/examples/cognitive_verifier.lang
languages/whence/examples/cognitive_verifier_v2.lang
languages/whence/examples/cognitive_verifier_v3.lang
languages/whence/examples/expense_tracker.lang
languages/whence/examples/mini_agi_guardian.lang
languages/whence/examples/nano_reasoner.lang
languages/whence/examples/prod_demo_v1.lang
languages/whence/examples/prod_demo_v3.lang
languages/whence/examples/prod_demo_v4.lang
languages/whence/examples/prod_demo_v5.lang
languages/whence/examples/prod_showcase_final.lang
languages/whence/examples/test_simple.lang
languages/whence/examples/whenceguard_auditor.lang
languages/whence/examples/whenceguard_v2.lang
languages/whence/examples/agi_buy_and_hold.lang
# Round 473 (SWE-loop D): a SIXTH per-round log, and the FOURTH time in a row
# a per-round log was wired without its ignore line (rounds 363/365, 409,
# 441, and now). `run_driver.sh:752` writes
# `logs/whenceslow_round_<N>.log` for every round the whence slow-tier slice
# runs in — round 469 added the slice and the pattern below was not extended,
# so round 472's log landed in `git status` as an unattributed `??` and was
# reported to this round by the record-gap check.
#
# Checked before adding, by round 441's rule that an ignore line has readers
# beyond `git status`: `git grep -n whenceslow_round` returns exactly ONE
# in-tree hit outside `logs/` — the `run_driver.sh` line that writes it.
# Nothing selects on its git status, so ignoring it silences no measurement.
# The durable artefact is `state/whence-slow-ledger.jsonl`, which is tracked,
# and `driver.log` already carries the slice's summary line.
logs/whenceslow_round_*.log
